  "head_commit": {
    "id": "22a29b30dee3b3930cf49bba50454650c31d2a07",
    "tree_id": "8d63e45b1ee981e222644723c77c486efc821a88",
    "message": "fix: resolve uuid refs in search results, breadcrumbs, and nested page refs (#13580)\n\n* fix: resolve uuid refs in search result titles\n\n94ea551ec4 rewrote block-ref-id->title with (filter map? frontier),\nbut datascript entities are not map?, so recur-replace-uuid-in-block-title\nsilently stopped resolving refs for entity inputs (search index, search\nresults, breadcrumbs, export). ((uuid)) refs were additionally never\nmatched by the id-ref patterns or kept in :block/refs.\n\n- accept entities as well as maps when collecting ref titles\n- match ((uuid)) refs and replace them with the referenced title\n- include ((uuid)) in get-matched-ids so :block/refs stays complete\n- resolve ((uuid)) targets directly from the title instead of relying\n  on :block/refs\n- resolve search result titles in the worker through the entity, since\n  pulled result maps lack :block/refs\n\n* fix: resolve title id refs without :block/refs and rebuild index\n\n* refactor: drop (()) support; node refs resolve via [[uuid]] only\n\nBlock and page are both nodes in db graphs and node refs uniformly use\n[[uuid]], so (()) handling is removed from title resolution,\nget-matched-ids, and search. Search now only re-resolves ref titles when\nthe title matches [[uuid]].\n\n* fix: resolve nested uuid refs in breadcrumb titles\n\nBreadcrumbs showed raw [[uuid]] for title refs that are not in :block/refs,\ne.g. [[<foo-uuid>]] nested inside a page-ref name ([[[[foo]] bar]] nested).\n\n- worker :block-breadcrumb ref-titles now also resolves every [[uuid]] found\n  in ancestor titles via d/entity, transitively through ref titles, so the\n  payload covers nested id refs (and watches those entities).\n- with-breadcrumb-ref-titles appends shallow refs for ref-titles uuids that\n  are missing from :block/refs.\n- page breadcrumb segments resolve [[uuid]] in :block/title like block\n  segments already did.\n\n* fix: resolve nested uuid refs in breadcrumbs and page refs\n\nThe :block.temp/breadcrumb fast path dropped the worker-computed\n:ref-titles, so nested uuid refs (e.g. [[<uuid>]] inside a page-ref\nname) stayed raw in the header, page, sidebar, and search-result\nbreadcrumbs. Plumb :block.temp/breadcrumb-ref-titles alongside the\nancestors at every producer and read it back in breadcrumb.\n\nNested page refs like [[[[foo]] bar]] nested rendered the raw\nstored name [[<uuid>]] bar because nested-link printed :block/name\ndirectly. Look up the page by name via [:page-identity] and render\nthe resolved page title, falling back to the previous behavior for\nmissing pages.\n\nMove breadcrumb-ref-titles into frontend.worker.handler.block-breadcrumb\nso search results can attach :block.temp/breadcrumb-ref-titles too.\n\n* test: expect :block.temp/breadcrumb-ref-titles in first-paint page map\n\n* fix: resolve uuids nested inside breadcrumb ref titles",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-03T14:57:34Z",
